  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAfter a cold start, plenty of sunshine should help temps rebound\ninto the 50s for most areas this afternoon. Winds will be much\nlighter than Saturday, generally 5-15 mph.\n\nClear skies, light/calm winds and the dry air mass remaining in\nplace should allow for good radiational cooling again tonight,\nwith lows in the 20s to lower/mid 30s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDeveloping Nor'Easter off the mid Atlantic coast looks to\nmeander offshore through midweek, as strengthening mid/upper\nlevel ridging anchors north and west of the system. For our\nregion, this portends an extended period of dry weather and near\nseasonable temps through at least midweek. Far SE areas could \nsee occasional clouds and a slight uptick in winds Tuesday- \nWednesday around the NW periphery of the Nor'Easter, however \nlittle if any additional impacts are expected at this time \nassuming the system remains far enough offshore, which most of \nthe physical model/AI ensembles currently suggest.",
